00:17:09.655 --> 00:17:11.255
departments might like.

00:17:12.215 --> 00:17:17.735
A nice thing about QuickBooks here is you can print a budget to actual report

00:17:17.895 --> 00:17:22.520
per department. Department. So if you only wanted the department for

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.280
instrumental

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:25.240
assistance,

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:30.040
you could print a report for just that department.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:42.065
Or if you wanted to combine a report for all of your one your zero zero zero which is your function code, you wanted to print the report only that,

00:17:42.225 --> 00:17:47.185
you can go in and prepare report based on specific criteria

00:17:47.585 --> 00:17:48.945
in specific

00:17:48.945 --> 00:17:49.585
accounts.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:57.000
Then the nice other nice thing is you can memorize it. So once you have a report, if it's a report that you're going to use

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.240
monthly or quarterly,

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.520
even weekly,

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.440
you can have a memorized report, you name it what you would like,

00:18:05.405 --> 00:18:09.645
and then you are able to pull it up, change the date,

00:18:10.285 --> 00:18:11.885
print it, save it,

00:18:12.285 --> 00:18:13.725
or just

00:18:13.885 --> 00:18:16.125
change anything at that time that you might like,

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.580
re memorize it, or change it after that.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:25.900
The next document I wanted to show you was the audit trail.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:34.415
Nice thing about QuickBooks, the audit trail is on at all times. It can never be shut off. In the earlier versions,

00:18:34.575 --> 00:18:36.575
you could turn the audit trail on

00:18:36.815 --> 00:18:40.095
and shut it off at will. Anybody could do it.

00:18:40.415 --> 00:18:46.200
At this point now, it's always on. How the audit trail works is once

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:48.120
a user

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.120
is signed on

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:55.480
and if they have credentials in order to be able to enter

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.625
information in, It automatically records,

00:18:58.625 --> 00:19:02.305
as you can see, the date and the time and who entered it.

00:19:03.105 --> 00:19:05.985
If that person also has the ability

00:19:06.225 --> 00:19:07.505
to change

00:19:07.905 --> 00:19:09.185
their own numbers,

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:12.490
it will show the original

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.290
document or the original transaction

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:18.650
and then it will also show the change

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:19.930
who did the change

00:19:22.845 --> 00:19:25.245
person who entered the date and the time.

00:19:26.045 --> 00:19:31.085
Can't be shut off, it's always there and you find it up in the report section.

00:19:31.325 --> 00:19:41.570
And I use this report quite often when I'm going to a client if I'm looking for a reason why maybe something no longer reconciles on the bank account

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:45.810
and I have a general idea, I can pull this report

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:49.330
for a day period, a month period, a week period,

00:19:49.835 --> 00:19:53.275
any set period that has information in the QuickBooks,

00:19:53.515 --> 00:19:56.795
I can pull a report and track

00:19:57.195 --> 00:19:58.955
what might have changed

00:19:59.195 --> 00:20:01.035
to cause the books to go

00:20:01.755 --> 00:20:02.875
out of balance.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:08.750
Any questions so far on the budget to actual

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:10.910
and or the audit trail?

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.150
No. Okay.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:18.615
The next report that I sent over

