and go about whatever business they are allowed to

00:20:55.715 --> 00:20:56.675
provide.

00:20:57.075 --> 00:20:58.355
As you scroll down,

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.030
I gave you

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.270
the normal

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:03.470
features

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:06.830
that a person can be given.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.990
The first thing it asks you, what what areas do you want them to have?

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.390
In this case, I made sure to select

00:21:13.695 --> 00:21:14.175
the,

00:21:14.655 --> 00:21:16.095
select areas.

00:21:16.095 --> 00:21:24.255
If you have somebody, maybe your treasurer would have full access, someone else may have select, and then it says sales are receivable.

00:21:24.335 --> 00:21:26.095
Although you don't necessarily

00:21:26.095 --> 00:21:27.375
have receivables,

00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:29.280
the school might have receivables

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:31.520
if they are billing out

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:38.400
maybe a pre k program that the parents are contributing to. You can be running your invoices

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.920
through QuickBooks also. You may want somebody to be able to

00:21:42.625 --> 00:21:44.305
record the transaction,

00:21:44.545 --> 00:21:50.625
you may not want them to be able to change the transaction and that's where you can set that criteria.

00:21:50.945 --> 00:21:52.065
Purchase orders,

00:21:52.225 --> 00:21:55.185
I know that the school uses purchase orders,

00:21:55.425 --> 00:22:00.610
the town I believe attempts or does use, not quite sure if you use purchase orders or not.

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:04.610
QuickBooks does have purchase orders and we'll get into that in a minute,

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:07.730
but here also you can set the rights

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:10.850
of that particular person, in this case the bookkeeper,

00:22:11.115 --> 00:22:16.475
on what they can do with their transaction and what they cannot do within their transaction.

00:22:18.795 --> 00:22:22.795
Checking and credit cards, although you don't receive probably credit card payments,

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:26.820
although you probably do for your tax collector and maybe your town clerk,

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:29.540
you can set the access

00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:30.820
on

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:33.220
those types of transactions also,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:35.220
or no criteria.

00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:37.780
They can have full access.

00:22:38.335 --> 00:22:42.895
You don't normally have inventory, but that's part of the program.

00:22:43.375 --> 00:22:57.470
Time tracking. I know I was asked if QuickBooks does do time tracking. Yes, it does. You can track time. You could have somebody enter in the time. And there are several programs that link. QuickBooks has its own separate program that will link

00:22:58.590 --> 00:23:02.350
an employee's time sheet, right, to QuickBooks.

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:04.430
If you decide to do in house

00:23:04.590 --> 00:23:05.550
payroll,

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:09.195
it has that ability to do that also.

00:23:10.315 --> 00:23:11.835
Payroll employees,

00:23:11.915 --> 00:23:12.875
time tracking,

00:23:13.115 --> 00:23:14.635
sensitive accounting.

00:23:15.195 --> 00:23:18.475
This is where you decide who can see what reports.

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:20.640
Can they change

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:29.040
items? Can they not change items? Can they only print? Can they only enter? You get to decide what that person's criteria

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:29.680
is.

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:31.1000
There's additional reporting

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.080
activities,

00:23:34.745 --> 00:23:37.385
changing and deleting transactions,

00:23:37.945 --> 00:23:40.025
which is potentially a large one.

00:23:40.425 --> 00:23:45.705
Remember though, audit trail on, even if an employee has

00:23:45.785 --> 00:23:46.985
the ability

00:23:47.465 --> 00:23:48.985
to delete or change

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:50.980
a transaction

00:23:51.140 --> 00:23:53.060
still going to be recorded

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:54.900
in the audit trail.

00:23:55.540 --> 00:23:58.180
So if someone makes an improper

00:23:58.180 --> 00:23:59.220
correction,

00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:03.620
at least you'll be able to track it and decide how you need to fix it going forward.

00:24:06.275 --> 00:24:07.235
The final

00:24:07.635 --> 00:24:10.355
accounts screen will be and there's

00:24:10.355 --> 00:24:12.675
another page, so they only gave me that one snapshot

00:24:13.075 --> 00:24:15.955
all of the rights of that particular person.

00:24:16.755 --> 00:24:20.355
You can change them at any time you want. So the bookkeeper

00:24:20.355 --> 00:24:21.235
has

00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:23.870
a specific set of criteria,

00:24:24.990 --> 00:24:26.670
the treasurer or

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:31.550
the town administrator decides that this person needs to have additional

00:24:33.550 --> 00:24:34.030
activities,

00:24:34.635 --> 00:24:35.515
rights,

00:24:35.675 --> 00:24:40.075
you can always go back in. The admin can always make changes.

00:24:40.315 --> 00:24:43.035
Only the admin can change

00:24:43.275 --> 00:24:45.595
a person's rights within QuickBooks.

00:24:45.675 --> 00:24:46.795
No one else can.

00:24:47.035 --> 00:24:49.835
We normally like the admin to be a separate

00:24:51.370 --> 00:24:54.090
person that's not utilized

00:24:54.250 --> 00:24:56.650
except to add users,

00:24:57.050 --> 00:24:58.410
correct users.

00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:01.290
And I personally like the admin

00:25:01.290 --> 00:25:03.770
to be the person entering in the budget,

00:25:04.505 --> 00:25:08.345
maybe making line item transfers or additional appropriations.

00:25:08.585 --> 00:25:11.465
In this case you might prefer that the treasurer do that.

00:25:12.905 --> 00:25:19.640
And then once the reports are ready to go to the auditor and if the auditor has any adjusting entries,

00:25:20.920 --> 00:25:24.040
the admin person whoever is assigned those rights

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:29.400
would then go in and record any adjusting entries that the auditor may have.

00:25:31.995 --> 00:25:34.315
Any questions so far for that?

00:25:35.595 --> 00:25:36.795
No? Okay.

00:25:37.195 --> 00:25:38.955
So some of your

00:25:39.275 --> 00:25:42.075
I'm going down my list. I have it here on my phone.

00:25:45.355 --> 00:25:46.155
Limitations

00:25:46.155 --> 00:25:47.035
for QuickBooks.

00:25:49.920 --> 00:25:51.120
The seven

00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:53.120
digit account number

00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:55.600
certainly can be a concern

00:25:55.920 --> 00:25:56.800
for

00:25:57.360 --> 00:25:58.320
the school.

00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:00.560
I'm not sure whether

00:26:00.640 --> 00:26:02.480
the town uses

00:26:02.695 --> 00:26:06.135
a 22 digit account number or not,

00:26:07.895 --> 00:26:10.135
but they only allow seven digits.

00:26:10.935 --> 00:26:18.790
I do know some of the other programs that will be looked at tonight also do allow for a longer or a larger set

00:26:18.870 --> 00:26:20.470
of account numbers.

00:26:21.350 --> 00:26:22.870
QuickBooks does not.

00:26:25.590 --> 00:26:27.430
I am not aware

00:26:27.430 --> 00:26:31.295
of any school districts at this time that are using QuickBooks.

00:26:31.615 --> 00:26:35.215
I went out and did an extensive search

00:26:35.295 --> 00:26:37.615
attempting to see if I could find

00:26:37.935 --> 00:26:38.655
any

00:26:39.775 --> 00:26:44.320
school districts that were utilizing it, but I did not uncover any.

00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:50.720
Many of the smaller towns, whether it's in Connecticut or one of the other states do use QuickBooks.

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:53.040
Most of their

00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:54.160
chart of accounts,

00:26:54.985 --> 00:26:57.065
trial balance are smaller

00:26:57.865 --> 00:26:58.665
and

00:26:58.985 --> 00:27:00.665
don't have as many

00:27:01.225 --> 00:27:02.265
sub accounts

00:27:02.425 --> 00:27:04.105
sometimes as the school.

00:27:04.825 --> 00:27:05.625
But

00:27:06.425 --> 00:27:08.025
that is what I had found.

00:27:11.120 --> 00:27:12.800
The chart of accounts

00:27:13.600 --> 00:27:16.080
does give us the availability though

00:27:17.040 --> 00:27:17.840
of

00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:20.560
deciding

00:27:21.215 --> 00:27:24.095
the account numbers that work best

00:27:24.335 --> 00:27:25.615
for the town

00:27:25.855 --> 00:27:30.735
and the Board of Education if that's the route that everyone decides to go.

00:27:31.375 --> 00:27:34.255
And then you would use the State of Connecticut

00:27:34.415 --> 00:27:35.615
mapping program.

00:27:36.510 --> 00:27:38.430
Once you have your account numbers,

00:27:38.670 --> 00:27:40.830
it would be an Excel spreadsheet

00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:44.510
that would have the town or the school's

00:27:45.710 --> 00:27:52.225
chart of accounts in there, including the balance sheet. Balance sheet has to be mapped and uploaded to the state also.

00:27:52.625 --> 00:27:55.185
And then a separate tab would show

00:27:56.785 --> 00:27:58.945
the combining effect

00:27:59.425 --> 00:28:01.185
of the QuickBooks file

00:28:01.930 --> 00:28:03.450
to an appropriate

00:28:05.530 --> 00:28:06.250
format

00:28:06.330 --> 00:28:09.210
that then can be uploaded by itself

00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:10.730
to the

00:28:10.970 --> 00:28:12.250
State of Connecticut site.

00:28:15.805 --> 00:28:17.885
They do fund accounting.

00:28:18.205 --> 00:28:22.445
It can, but it does not do reciprocal

00:28:22.445 --> 00:28:23.965
due to, due froms.

00:28:24.285 --> 00:28:25.965
So what I mean by that,

00:28:26.605 --> 00:28:34.900
let's say and I don't I'm not picking on the Board of Education or it could be let I won't do that. Let's say the town. Say the town

00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:36.500
pays an invoice,

00:28:36.900 --> 00:28:39.060
and that invoice is a combination

00:28:39.300 --> 00:28:41.780
of normal road maintenance

00:28:42.260 --> 00:28:44.740
for the town under public works,

00:28:44.980 --> 00:28:47.855
but also has a capital nonrecurring

00:28:47.855 --> 00:28:48.815
component.

00:28:49.775 --> 00:28:51.055
In your Phoenix,

00:28:51.375 --> 00:28:53.375
when you recorded that transaction,

00:28:53.615 --> 00:28:55.215
it would automatically

00:28:55.775 --> 00:28:57.535
record the public works

00:28:57.935 --> 00:28:59.295
portion of the transaction,

00:28:59.780 --> 00:29:03.220
but it would set up in the due to, due from

00:29:03.940 --> 00:29:06.260
of the Phoenix and would automatically

00:29:06.260 --> 00:29:09.780
go in to the capital not reoccurring fund

00:29:10.580 --> 00:29:12.180
and record the transaction

00:29:12.825 --> 00:29:19.145
for that particular asset or what have you that's going to be recorded there. QuickBooks will not do that.

00:29:19.785 --> 00:29:25.625
You will have have due to, due froms, whether it's for the school, capital non recurring,

00:29:26.425 --> 00:29:28.825
any of your smaller funds, your library

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:31.840
funds, things of that nature, you'll have to have separate

00:29:31.840 --> 00:29:33.600
due to, due froms

00:29:34.320 --> 00:29:36.080
within potentially

00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:38.080
within your QuickBooks.

00:29:38.640 --> 00:29:41.440
And then you will have a separate QuickBooks

00:29:41.440 --> 00:29:43.280
file

00:29:42.845 --> 00:29:44.685
for those smaller

00:29:44.685 --> 00:29:45.485
funds.

00:29:46.125 --> 00:29:47.725
You can group them together.

00:29:48.525 --> 00:29:49.725
They appear

00:29:49.885 --> 00:29:51.005
on your

00:29:51.245 --> 00:29:52.445
audit report

00:29:52.525 --> 00:29:56.700
under non major funds. You could have multiple QuickBooks files.

00:29:56.780 --> 00:29:58.700
You could have one QuickBooks file.

00:29:58.780 --> 00:30:01.180
You can combine QuickBooks files.

00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:02.540
You could have any

00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:05.260
number of QuickBooks files that you might like

00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:06.780
on the system.

00:30:07.340 --> 00:30:12.175
It just will not do the due to, due from. You would physically have to print the report

00:30:12.895 --> 00:30:14.415
or have it open,

00:30:14.895 --> 00:30:18.575
go into the other fund and record those transactions.

00:30:21.935 --> 00:30:22.735
Purchase orders.

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:24.920
QuickBooks will

00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:26.760
do purchase orders,

00:30:28.120 --> 00:30:29.880
but it is not ideal.

00:30:30.120 --> 00:30:36.920
So QuickBooks will allow you to prepare a purchase order, but QuickBooks considers that a non

00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:37.880
posting

00:30:38.315 --> 00:30:39.275
transaction.

00:30:41.035 --> 00:30:45.115
In order for it to show up on your budget to actual,

00:30:45.355 --> 00:30:52.880
which obviously is very important because that's your mechanism to make sure that departments do not overextend

00:30:52.880 --> 00:30:54.080
their budget.

00:30:55.200 --> 00:30:58.560
You potentially might have to have two separate reports,

00:30:58.640 --> 00:31:00.400
budget to actual reports,

00:31:00.640 --> 00:31:02.240
and have them memorized.

00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:05.040
One of the reports is going to show

00:31:07.115 --> 00:31:09.195
non posted transactions,

00:31:09.595 --> 00:31:10.955
which are your

00:31:11.035 --> 00:31:12.155
purchase orders.

00:31:12.395 --> 00:31:14.075
If you have a non

00:31:15.035 --> 00:31:16.635
posting transaction

00:31:16.715 --> 00:31:18.315
within the budget to actual,

00:31:18.730 --> 00:31:21.930
it will show the total amount of the purchase order.

00:31:22.890 --> 00:31:26.090
Then once you have paid that

00:31:27.130 --> 00:31:28.410
purchase order

00:31:29.050 --> 00:31:32.730
through the pay bills feature, once the bill is received,

00:31:33.385 --> 00:31:35.545
you would have to have a separate report

00:31:36.025 --> 00:31:37.705
that would show

00:31:38.345 --> 00:31:39.785
paid items.

00:31:40.425 --> 00:31:43.545
I did try to print a report

00:31:43.625 --> 00:31:48.265
that showed both non posting and posting items within the QuickBooks,

00:31:48.780 --> 00:31:50.620
and it doubled the amount.

00:31:50.860 --> 00:31:53.340
So I put in a transaction for

00:31:53.500 --> 00:31:54.620
17,000

00:31:54.620 --> 00:31:55.980
as a purchase order,

00:31:56.940 --> 00:31:59.580
showed it as a non posted transaction.

00:31:59.740 --> 00:32:01.820
Then I went in and recorded

00:32:01.820 --> 00:32:03.580
receipt of the invoice

00:32:04.015 --> 00:32:06.095
for $17,000

00:32:06.415 --> 00:32:07.775
went back in,

00:32:08.095 --> 00:32:15.855
did a posting either or either a non posted or a posting item, and it made that line item look like it had $34,000

00:32:15.855 --> 00:32:17.055
of an expenditure,

00:32:17.215 --> 00:32:19.135
when in truth it only had 17.

00:32:20.530 --> 00:32:26.690
As I tried to work through the problem, I found that potentially two reports would be necessary,

00:32:26.850 --> 00:32:27.890
a posting

00:32:28.050 --> 00:32:31.890
report for one and potentially a non posting report for the other.

00:32:33.165 --> 00:32:34.125
QuickBooks

00:32:34.765 --> 00:32:38.605
does also have some other programs that it will

00:32:39.725 --> 00:32:40.765
sync with.

00:32:41.325 --> 00:32:44.845
So if you wanted to have the purchase orders prepared

00:32:45.390 --> 00:32:47.790
and have the department head

00:32:47.870 --> 00:32:51.630
approve them, you would need to use an outside

00:32:52.590 --> 00:32:53.470
supplier,

00:32:53.790 --> 00:32:55.470
another software company.

00:32:55.710 --> 00:32:58.590
But the same thing will happen once you

00:32:58.865 --> 00:33:01.105
bring it into QuickBooks.

00:33:01.585 --> 00:33:04.945
It's still considered a non posting transaction.

00:33:05.985 --> 00:33:10.545
